WEBVTT

00:00:01.117 --> 00:00:05.987
Yume kara samete mo
Even if I wake from my dreams

00:00:07.027 --> 00:00:12.357
Kono te wo nobasu yo
I'll reach my hand out to you

00:00:24.007 --> 00:00:29.277
Onaji tsuyosa de yobi au
If our hearts can reach each other

00:00:30.017 --> 00:00:34.777
Kokoro ni nareru no naraba
with the same strength

00:00:35.957 --> 00:00:41.217
Nanninbun no kizu demo
Then I would be able to bare

00:00:41.757 --> 00:00:46.887
Boku wa uketome rareru yo
The pain of many hearts

00:00:47.297 --> 00:00:50.827
Mousukoshi datte kiga surun da
I can feel that it will arrive soon

00:00:50.897 --> 00:00:55.997
Kono kabe ga kuzureru
When these walls will be torn down

00:00:56.637 --> 00:01:01.137
Reimei
The dawn

00:01:02.717 --> 00:01:08.677
Yume kara samete mo
mada minai yume no houmade
Even if we wake from our dreams
We'll have to keep running

00:01:08.757 --> 00:01:14.657
Bokura wa hitori de
hashiri tsuzukeru shika nain da
Towards our unrevealed dreams

00:01:14.727 --> 00:01:21.287
Korogari mayotte tsukuri dasu
boku no inryoku ga
The gravity by my painful journey
will draw me

00:01:21.567 --> 00:01:27.437
Itsuka kimi e
To you one day

00:01:56.667 --> 00:01:58.067
Hey, are you okay?

00:01:58.367 --> 00:01:59.397
What happened?

00:02:02.137 --> 00:02:03.197
Tri-Edge!

00:02:07.347 --> 00:02:08.607
Tri-Edge?

00:02:14.617 --> 00:02:18.417
Hey, did you know there's
a PC that got away from Tri-Edge?

00:02:18.487 --> 00:02:21.257
Of course! If everyone he's met
just became a Lost One...

00:02:21.327 --> 00:02:22.987
...nobody would
be talking about this.

00:02:23.157 --> 00:02:24.527
Yeah, I guess that's true.

00:02:24.827 --> 00:02:26.297
So, who was it?

00:02:26.397 --> 00:02:28.527
It wasn't that
Black Multi-Weapon, was it?

00:02:28.597 --> 00:02:31.067
No, it was a Blue Brandish.

00:02:31.137 --> 00:02:32.107
Really?

00:02:32.737 --> 00:02:33.897
The one that got away...

00:02:33.967 --> 00:02:37.377
...I think is that stuffed animal
who sits by the canal.

00:02:37.677 --> 00:02:42.207
Yeah, but he's a Warlock
and he's more brown than blue.

00:02:42.617 --> 00:02:43.667
I guess.

00:02:44.347 --> 00:02:46.907
I'm going to the port
to gather some information.

00:02:54.727 --> 00:02:57.127
It's definitely this PC.

00:02:57.197 --> 00:02:59.857
So, she escaped Tri-Edge.

00:03:00.127 --> 00:03:02.097
She looks like
a rare character.

00:03:02.197 --> 00:03:04.997
She is a legitimate character, though.

00:03:05.367 --> 00:03:06.807
Tri-Edge...

00:03:06.867 --> 00:03:08.167
The Lost Ones...

00:03:08.237 --> 00:03:10.837
And a series
of mysterious phenomena.

00:03:11.207 --> 00:03:17.377
Is this PC just another player
that got swept up in the current?

00:03:17.617 --> 00:03:18.917
Or...

00:03:19.487 --> 00:03:21.077
What would you
like me to do?

00:03:21.717 --> 00:03:23.347
- Pi.
- Yes.

00:03:23.417 --> 00:03:27.047
Think like Ovan
and act like Ovan.

00:03:28.227 --> 00:03:29.197
Yes.

00:03:48.647 --> 00:03:49.977
Phyllo's not here?

00:03:51.417 --> 00:03:52.387
Hey!

00:03:52.817 --> 00:03:54.647
I haven't seen him yet today.

00:03:54.717 --> 00:03:55.687
Oh.

00:03:56.187 --> 00:03:59.417
He's usually here,
so it's weird when he isn't.

00:04:00.827 --> 00:04:02.227
Is something the matter?

00:04:03.827 --> 00:04:05.527
Can I talk to you
about something?

00:04:05.597 --> 00:04:06.657
Sure.

00:04:06.867 --> 00:04:07.987
I...

00:04:09.697 --> 00:04:12.397
...wonder what Shino would do.

00:04:13.707 --> 00:04:19.107
I've been thinking this whole time
about what it is that I can do...

00:04:20.507 --> 00:04:23.847
But no matter how hard I try,
I can't be like Shino.

00:04:24.747 --> 00:04:27.947
So, I think I should do my best
at what I can do.

00:04:28.217 --> 00:04:29.587
And what would that be?

00:04:30.017 --> 00:04:32.387
I don't know...

00:04:32.457 --> 00:04:34.587
That's why I came
to seek Phyllo's advice.

00:04:38.367 --> 00:04:40.797
You should be a guild master.

00:04:40.867 --> 00:04:41.927
Huh?

00:04:42.367 --> 00:04:45.567
There are things you can do
in a team that you can't do alone.

00:04:45.907 --> 00:04:47.807
Just form a guild for now.

00:04:49.077 --> 00:04:50.537
That's where it starts.

00:05:07.727 --> 00:05:09.417
Too bad.

00:05:09.497 --> 00:05:12.397
I'm telling you that
you're no match for me.

00:05:12.467 --> 00:05:15.827
You don't know that
until you try us.

00:05:16.097 --> 00:05:17.897
Are the rumors false?

00:05:27.347 --> 00:05:29.977
Apparently you know Tri-Edge.

00:05:30.877 --> 00:05:31.907
Master Yata.

00:05:38.657 --> 00:05:41.487
This is beyond anything
we could have expected.

00:06:03.017 --> 00:06:04.637
Is that all?

00:06:11.457 --> 00:06:12.757
Damn!

00:06:12.827 --> 00:06:16.347
I can't get that guy
out of my head.

00:06:25.107 --> 00:06:28.037
You can't resolve this
by using your strength.

00:06:28.207 --> 00:06:29.267
You're wrong.

00:06:29.337 --> 00:06:32.567
I am what I am
because I use my strength.

00:06:33.077 --> 00:06:34.137
Meaning?

00:06:34.207 --> 00:06:36.437
We're wasting time
talking about it.

00:06:36.547 --> 00:06:37.947
One minute, right?

00:06:38.017 --> 00:06:39.537
My "hit-me-if-you-can" service?

00:06:39.617 --> 00:06:40.707
How much?

00:06:41.147 --> 00:06:45.177
If you become a regular customer,
then the first one's free.

00:06:45.887 --> 00:06:48.947
So, that's why
I started a guild...

00:06:49.697 --> 00:06:51.757
...but I still don't know
what to do.

00:06:52.427 --> 00:06:54.557
I think you should
think things in order.

00:06:54.627 --> 00:06:55.657
Huh?

00:06:55.767 --> 00:06:57.737
First, what is it
that you want to do?

00:07:00.507 --> 00:07:02.367
I want to help Haseo.

00:07:02.437 --> 00:07:03.737
What do you mean by "help"?

00:07:03.837 --> 00:07:06.967
I think I'm capable of healing people.

00:07:07.047 --> 00:07:08.667
Not just Haseo...

00:07:08.747 --> 00:07:12.407
...but I can revive those
who've been killed by Haseo, too.

00:07:12.947 --> 00:07:15.917
Healing is not a job
for a Grappler.

00:07:16.217 --> 00:07:19.777
But if I carried
as many items as I can...

00:07:19.857 --> 00:07:22.517
You'll never have enough
money for that.

00:07:23.427 --> 00:07:24.487
I guess so.

00:07:24.797 --> 00:07:27.267
But you asked me what I want to do.

00:07:29.097 --> 00:07:30.087
Yeah.

00:07:30.267 --> 00:07:31.567
You're right.

00:07:32.507 --> 00:07:36.097
Second, you need to figure out
how to achieve that.

00:07:37.777 --> 00:07:39.077
I don't know.

00:07:41.977 --> 00:07:43.177
I'll help you.

00:07:43.247 --> 00:07:44.217
Huh?

00:07:45.987 --> 00:07:48.447
I'll do whatever
I can for you.

00:07:48.817 --> 00:07:50.717
So, let's do our best together.

00:08:12.177 --> 00:08:13.477
That's it.

00:08:13.547 --> 00:08:14.807
One minute is up.

00:08:16.747 --> 00:08:18.337
So, that's it.

00:08:18.417 --> 00:08:20.007
Master Yata, look at this.

00:08:24.317 --> 00:08:27.087
I checked her past log.

00:08:27.827 --> 00:08:31.457
- It's here at Briona Gwydion.
- Give me the gist of it.

00:08:31.527 --> 00:08:33.467
Please wait.
There's one more.

00:08:35.237 --> 00:08:39.067
This is the log of Tri-Edge
and Ovan's battle.

00:08:40.937 --> 00:08:43.637
Same place. Same time.

00:08:44.577 --> 00:08:50.017
In other words, she witnessed
the battle of Tri-Edge and Ovan.

00:08:50.317 --> 00:08:51.577
Interesting.

00:08:51.647 --> 00:08:53.947
But that already happened.

00:08:54.687 --> 00:08:57.587
What are you going to do
with this information, Pi?

00:08:57.657 --> 00:09:01.527
I will think like Ovan
and I will act like Ovan.

00:09:02.357 --> 00:09:03.517
Welcome back.

00:09:04.227 --> 00:09:05.427
"Hit-me-if-you-can".

00:09:05.497 --> 00:09:06.467
Huh?

00:09:06.527 --> 00:09:09.657
The survivor Midori runs
a "hit-me-if-you-can" service.

00:09:09.767 --> 00:09:11.197
"Hit-me-if-you-can"?

00:09:12.307 --> 00:09:16.107
Basically, she invites people
to try and attack her.

00:09:16.177 --> 00:09:18.537
No, I still don't understand.

00:09:18.807 --> 00:09:22.537
She bets on herself
and fights PKs.

00:09:22.647 --> 00:09:26.517
If you can land even one hit,
you win some prize money.

00:09:26.787 --> 00:09:30.917
It must be the end of the world
for a business like that to succeed.

00:09:30.987 --> 00:09:32.517
Her business is doing well?

00:09:32.587 --> 00:09:34.387
Seems like it.

00:09:35.227 --> 00:09:36.317
Welcome!

00:09:38.027 --> 00:09:38.997
Where's Tohta?

00:09:39.067 --> 00:09:40.047
Do you know him?

00:09:40.127 --> 00:09:41.187
Sort of...

00:09:41.467 --> 00:09:44.027
I came to offer
some information.

00:09:44.097 --> 00:09:46.727
We don't buy information here.

00:09:47.567 --> 00:09:49.337
I'm not selling it.

00:09:49.437 --> 00:09:51.337
I said "offer",
didn't I?

00:09:51.707 --> 00:09:53.607
No, that won't do.

00:09:53.747 --> 00:09:56.177
There's nothing more expensive
than what's free.

00:09:56.247 --> 00:09:58.907
I'm not offering it to you.

00:09:58.987 --> 00:10:01.977
Tohta should be the one
to make that decision, right?

00:10:02.057 --> 00:10:03.217
Yeah, I guess.

00:10:05.057 --> 00:10:08.217
So, do you want to
hear it or not?

00:10:45.227 --> 00:10:46.527
Look, you!

00:10:46.597 --> 00:10:48.497
You can have this
PC body back.

00:10:48.567 --> 00:10:49.757
What should I do?

00:10:49.837 --> 00:10:52.127
If I log out,
will that do the trick?

00:10:52.207 --> 00:10:53.097
Huh?

00:10:53.167 --> 00:10:55.137
You said you wanted
to use it, right?

00:10:55.807 --> 00:10:57.397
So I'm giving it back.

00:10:57.707 --> 00:10:59.267
What are you up to?

00:10:59.347 --> 00:11:00.307
Nothing.

00:11:00.377 --> 00:11:03.607
Isn't it better to have a cheap car
that you can use when you want...

00:11:03.677 --> 00:11:07.307
...than a pricey one that might be
taken from you at any moment?

00:11:07.487 --> 00:11:09.317
I actually understand
you for once.

00:11:09.387 --> 00:11:10.577
So?

00:11:10.657 --> 00:11:13.987
What are you planning to do
with your cheap car?

00:11:14.557 --> 00:11:15.547
Here's a clue.

00:11:15.627 --> 00:11:16.747
Haseo.

00:11:18.397 --> 00:11:20.697
I'd like to watch him
a bit more.

00:11:21.267 --> 00:11:23.127
- I don't need it.
- What?

00:11:23.197 --> 00:11:26.397
That PC body is useless.
You can have it.

00:11:26.467 --> 00:11:27.437
Why?

00:11:27.867 --> 00:11:30.037
I told you it's useless now.

00:11:30.437 --> 00:11:32.837
I said I don't need it either.

00:11:32.907 --> 00:11:35.007
No matter how long
you keep sour milk...

00:11:35.077 --> 00:11:37.237
...you'll never
taste it again, right?

00:11:37.317 --> 00:11:39.407
Even if it ferments
and turns into cheese...

00:11:39.487 --> 00:11:43.247
...that's not the original...
- Oh, I take back what I said!

00:11:43.317 --> 00:11:45.987
I've had enough of your
stupid metaphors!

00:11:46.257 --> 00:11:47.517
Really?

00:11:47.587 --> 00:11:50.257
I'm giving you that PC body...

00:11:50.327 --> 00:11:52.357
...so don't come
near me anymore!

00:11:53.967 --> 00:11:56.697
Are those the conditions
for my freedom?

00:12:01.037 --> 00:12:05.377
She lashes out like a little brat.

00:12:12.347 --> 00:12:13.317
Hi!

00:12:13.517 --> 00:12:14.887
How's business?

00:12:15.417 --> 00:12:16.787
Oh, Tohta!

00:12:16.987 --> 00:12:19.047
We got amazing information!

00:12:20.087 --> 00:12:22.527
About the player
who witnessed the battle...

00:12:22.597 --> 00:12:24.387
...between Tri-Edge
and another PC.

00:12:24.727 --> 00:12:26.057
You know who it is?

00:12:26.367 --> 00:12:30.457
And that player
actually fought Tri-Edge, too!

00:12:30.537 --> 00:12:34.057
So this PC's a witness
and a survivor.

00:12:34.767 --> 00:12:35.667
What's the PC's name?

00:12:35.737 --> 00:12:36.607
Midori.

00:12:36.677 --> 00:12:37.727
Midori...

00:12:37.907 --> 00:12:39.997
Is she logged in
right now?

00:12:40.177 --> 00:12:42.207
She has a very strange business.

00:12:42.317 --> 00:12:44.647
She runs a
"hit-me-if-you-can" service.

00:12:44.717 --> 00:12:46.507
Who gave you this information?

00:12:46.587 --> 00:12:47.707
Pi.

00:12:47.787 --> 00:12:49.807
She has pink pigtails.

00:12:49.887 --> 00:12:51.117
Don't you know her?

00:12:51.287 --> 00:12:53.417
She seemed to know you.

00:12:54.787 --> 00:12:57.847
You should go thank her
if you do know her.

00:12:57.927 --> 00:13:00.757
And she seemed to know
that we were looking into it as well.

00:13:01.067 --> 00:13:02.757
I'll be back in a bit.

00:13:20.447 --> 00:13:21.437
Why?

00:13:22.287 --> 00:13:23.407
Why is it?

00:13:23.857 --> 00:13:27.687
Why did Midori meet Tri-Edge
and I can't?

00:13:36.567 --> 00:13:39.437
Are you Midori, the one with
the "hit-me-if-you-can" service?

00:13:41.007 --> 00:13:42.237
And you are...?

00:13:42.307 --> 00:13:46.297
Well, you can call me Tohta,
the tip-off man.

00:13:46.847 --> 00:13:49.137
So you're here
doing business, too.

00:13:49.847 --> 00:13:52.037
There's something I want to ask you.

00:13:52.347 --> 00:13:53.277
What?

00:13:53.347 --> 00:13:55.377
Do you know Tri-Edge?

00:13:56.057 --> 00:13:57.677
That again, huh.

00:13:57.757 --> 00:13:58.987
Again?

00:13:59.057 --> 00:14:01.817
Someone else
asked me about that.

00:14:01.997 --> 00:14:03.787
You sure are popular.

00:14:04.557 --> 00:14:08.657
You're a survivor,
but you're also a witness.

00:14:09.137 --> 00:14:10.227
Isn't that right?

00:14:10.837 --> 00:14:12.167
What are you trying to say?

00:14:12.537 --> 00:14:16.067
You barely got away
from Tri-Edge.

00:14:17.277 --> 00:14:20.177
That's true, but what do you
mean by "witness"?

00:14:20.947 --> 00:14:24.937
Apparently you witnessed
a battle between Tri-Edge...

00:14:25.017 --> 00:14:27.177
...and a regular player.

00:14:47.337 --> 00:14:49.207
That information is correct.

00:14:51.737 --> 00:14:54.507
I met Tri-Edge twice.

00:14:54.577 --> 00:14:57.707
Or I should say I saw him
one of those times.

00:14:58.117 --> 00:15:00.107
Is that all you wanted
to ask me?

00:15:01.287 --> 00:15:04.377
What did the one fighting
Tri-Edge look like?

00:15:04.517 --> 00:15:06.217
How would I know?

00:15:06.557 --> 00:15:08.317
I was watching from afar.

00:15:08.387 --> 00:15:10.157
How about their
general features?

00:15:37.957 --> 00:15:39.447
I don't remember.

00:15:40.087 --> 00:15:42.987
He seemed to know.

00:15:43.797 --> 00:15:44.957
It was a guy?

00:15:45.057 --> 00:15:49.827
He knew his way around the
Lost Ground, "Briona Gwydion".

00:15:50.037 --> 00:15:51.127
I see.

00:15:52.507 --> 00:15:55.697
You won't get any more out of me,
no matter how hard you try.

00:15:55.777 --> 00:15:56.737
Okay.

00:15:59.207 --> 00:16:00.267
What is this?

00:16:00.347 --> 00:16:02.707
Gratitude for your information.

00:16:02.777 --> 00:16:04.367
Are you stupid?

00:16:04.447 --> 00:16:07.107
I answered your questions
out of kindness.

00:16:07.647 --> 00:16:11.317
This shows my gratitude
for your kindness.

00:16:11.387 --> 00:16:12.287
I don't want it.

00:16:12.287 --> 00:16:15.157
Then I owe you one.
I'll leave you alone now.

00:16:18.157 --> 00:16:21.687
Will Haseo now
fight Midori again?

00:16:21.767 --> 00:16:22.697
Yes.

00:16:22.767 --> 00:16:25.237
This time it won't be her
"hit-me-if-you-can" service.

00:16:25.307 --> 00:16:27.267
She'll be fighting
with all of her strength.

00:16:27.337 --> 00:16:28.897
Will it jolt him?

00:16:28.977 --> 00:16:30.567
It's worth a try.

00:16:31.677 --> 00:16:33.977
Isn't that the way
Ovan would think?

00:16:40.387 --> 00:16:41.077
Hey!

00:16:41.147 --> 00:16:42.517
Are you ready?

00:16:43.287 --> 00:16:44.147
Yup!

00:16:44.217 --> 00:16:46.747
You need to get rid
of that character.

00:16:46.827 --> 00:16:47.817
What?

00:16:47.887 --> 00:16:50.117
The impact of first impressions.

00:16:50.197 --> 00:16:51.957
Being compatible is important.

00:16:52.027 --> 00:16:53.997
Are you saying
I should remake myself?

00:16:54.067 --> 00:16:55.027
Yeah.

00:16:55.597 --> 00:16:56.757
What's your profession?

00:16:56.837 --> 00:16:57.997
I'm a Blade.

00:16:58.067 --> 00:17:00.557
Change your profession
to a Harvest.

00:17:00.637 --> 00:17:01.537
What?

00:17:01.607 --> 00:17:02.767
Me too?

00:17:02.837 --> 00:17:05.037
You've already created a guild...

00:17:05.107 --> 00:17:07.097
...so you can't change
your character.

00:17:07.177 --> 00:17:08.267
Oh.

00:17:08.477 --> 00:17:11.307
Is it just going to be
the two of you?

00:17:11.377 --> 00:17:12.477
Is that bad?

00:17:12.647 --> 00:17:15.117
What's the minimum
for a party?

00:17:15.187 --> 00:17:17.587
- Three.
- You're missing one.

00:17:17.657 --> 00:17:19.087
One more...

00:17:19.487 --> 00:17:20.687
How about Phyllo?

00:17:20.757 --> 00:17:22.187
Are you serious?

00:17:22.627 --> 00:17:23.987
I guess that won't work.

00:17:24.057 --> 00:17:25.257
Of course.

00:17:25.327 --> 00:17:27.317
If Phyllo was going to do
anything like that...

00:17:27.397 --> 00:17:29.597
...I'd have him help me first.

00:17:29.997 --> 00:17:31.557
One more person, huh?

00:17:31.837 --> 00:17:35.237
One of my real-world friends
said he'll start playing soon.

00:17:35.307 --> 00:17:37.397
Hideyo. I'll see if he wants to join.

00:17:37.477 --> 00:17:40.337
Hideyo? That's a very
old-fashioned name.

00:17:40.547 --> 00:17:41.407
And...

00:17:41.477 --> 00:17:42.447
Hm?

00:17:42.517 --> 00:17:44.037
I'll get rid of this character.

00:17:45.747 --> 00:17:46.807
It's okay.

00:17:46.887 --> 00:17:51.117
Right, once you have your team,
you'll need a catchphrase.

00:17:51.187 --> 00:17:52.447
Catchphrase?

00:17:52.557 --> 00:17:56.687
If you want to leave a legacy,
you need to have style.

00:17:56.827 --> 00:17:57.917
I see.

00:17:58.157 --> 00:18:00.857
- So, what's your guild name?
- Paw Pad Squadron!

00:18:00.927 --> 00:18:02.697
Paw Pad?

00:18:02.767 --> 00:18:05.167
The soft parts
of an animal's paw?

00:18:05.537 --> 00:18:06.507
Yeah.

00:18:07.007 --> 00:18:08.057
Is that bad?

00:18:09.407 --> 00:18:10.467
You pass!

00:18:29.557 --> 00:18:31.087
Sorry I'm late.

00:18:31.397 --> 00:18:33.057
So, what is it?

00:18:33.127 --> 00:18:37.127
There's a player who defeated
Tri-Edge at Briona Gwydion.

00:18:37.537 --> 00:18:38.597
Defeated?

00:18:39.107 --> 00:18:42.037
Does that mean
Tri-Edge is no longer around?!

00:18:42.107 --> 00:18:43.627
I don't know about that.

00:18:43.707 --> 00:18:44.767
Who was it?!

00:18:44.837 --> 00:18:46.677
Who is the guy
that defeated him?!

00:18:46.747 --> 00:18:47.737
I don't know.

00:18:47.807 --> 00:18:50.277
As long as the source of the
information doesn't remember...

00:18:50.347 --> 00:18:51.937
...I can't dig for it.

00:18:52.017 --> 00:18:53.577
Who told you this?

00:18:53.647 --> 00:18:54.777
Midori.

00:18:54.917 --> 00:18:57.007
That "hit-me-if-you-can" woman.

00:18:57.087 --> 00:18:58.177
Her!

00:18:58.657 --> 00:19:01.677
She's a survivor and a witness.

00:19:01.757 --> 00:19:04.587
That's what I've heard.
No, it's the other way around.

00:19:04.657 --> 00:19:06.857
She survived because
she was a witness.

00:19:06.927 --> 00:19:08.797
Now that's a possibility.

00:19:10.637 --> 00:19:11.797
Where are you going?

00:19:13.307 --> 00:19:14.707
Where do you think?

00:19:18.607 --> 00:19:20.807
I guess that was to be expected.

00:19:59.017 --> 00:20:00.507
What do you want this time?

00:20:00.787 --> 00:20:01.717
You!

00:20:01.787 --> 00:20:03.617
What do you know
about Tri-Edge?

00:20:03.687 --> 00:20:05.177
I already told you!

00:20:05.287 --> 00:20:08.817
You saw Tri-Edge
being defeated.

00:20:08.897 --> 00:20:09.947
And if I did?

00:20:10.027 --> 00:20:12.957
You better remember
the one who defeated him.

00:20:13.267 --> 00:20:15.757
No, I don't want to remember.

00:20:25.777 --> 00:20:27.297
I can smell death.

00:20:29.617 --> 00:20:33.377
I wish you'd take
the place of Tri-Edge.

00:20:45.767 --> 00:20:46.727
You're good.

00:20:46.797 --> 00:20:49.227
You're actually pretty good.

00:20:50.497 --> 00:20:54.227
Who are you?

00:20:54.807 --> 00:20:57.607
I told you.
I run a "hit-me-if-you-can" service.

00:21:31.707 --> 00:21:33.977
He was strong, that Tri-Edge.

00:21:34.707 --> 00:21:36.767
I guess you're just not.

00:21:37.647 --> 00:21:39.047
Whatever.

00:21:47.357 --> 00:21:49.787
The Factor is still dormant.

00:22:05.137 --> 00:22:12.737
I can't even defeat the one
who barely escaped Tri-Edge?

00:22:30.067 --> 00:22:33.657
Ikiru wa dokuhai kiyu no kurushimi wo
Life is a poisoned cup of needless suffering

00:22:33.737 --> 00:22:37.227
Nomihosu sube wo dare ga sazukeyo
That no one can show me how to drain

00:22:37.507 --> 00:22:40.907
Taiyo ni sumu toiu kenja no washi
A wise eagle is said to live in the sun

00:22:40.977 --> 00:22:45.347
Habataki dake ga kodama suru
The flapping of its wings
is all that echoes

00:22:48.787 --> 00:22:52.317
Kono futatsu no me ni yadotta
In each of these eyes

00:22:52.387 --> 00:22:56.087
Yami to Hikari sono docchi de
Dwell darkness and light

00:22:56.157 --> 00:23:03.397
Boku wa ashita wo mitsumeru
beki nano darou
Through which shall I look to tomorrow?

00:23:03.467 --> 00:23:07.127
Kawaki kitta gareki no machi
A dried out and ruined city

00:23:07.207 --> 00:23:10.897
Ten to sen wo tsunagi awase
Draws the lines between the dots

00:23:10.977 --> 00:23:17.907
Imi nado nai koto bakari afurete iku
Causing meaningless events to overflow

00:23:18.077 --> 00:23:21.747
Honou no gotoki kodoku
Soothing the loneliness

00:23:21.817 --> 00:23:24.847
Idaku karada shizumete wa
That flames up within the body

00:23:24.917 --> 00:23:32.457
Ankyo eto shitatatte iku shizuku
Droplets of water fall towards the culvert

00:23:32.697 --> 00:23:36.257
Kakageru dokuhai kono sei wa michitemo
Even if the poisoned cup is upheld
and filled with this life

00:23:36.367 --> 00:23:40.067
Kogareru shino yume wa nagare tsuku
My dream that yearns for death
drifts into it

00:23:40.267 --> 00:23:43.707
Toride ni kuikomu tsume kokou no washi
The eagle remains aloof;
its talons dig into the fort

00:23:43.777 --> 00:23:47.337
Habataki dake ga maiagaru
Only the flapping of its wings resounds

00:23:47.407 --> 00:23:51.137
Ano soukyu ni takkei ni shite kure tamae
Let me be crucified in the blue sky

00:23:51.217 --> 00:23:54.577
Ten to chi ga musubu basho ni
bokuwa tatsu
I'll stand where heaven and earth meet

00:23:55.917 --> 00:23:57.047
Next Episode
